# SEO And GEO Standard

Per-route title/description/OG rules: `@seo-metadata.mdc`.
Workflow: `.cursor/skills/seo-page-setup/SKILL.md`.
Human guide: `docs/guides/marketing-seo-geo.md`.

## Why this matters

- **Legacy search:** one canonical host (`www`), final URLs in the sitemap, unique metadata. Apex redirects must not appear as canonicals.
- **AI search / GEO:** answer engines cite pages they can fetch and attribute. JSON-LD, `/llms.txt`, and explicit crawl allow help OneTap appear in citations.
- **EN + HE:** every public English URL needs its Hebrew twin with hreflang.
- **Previews:** Vercel preview must stay `noindex` / robots `Disallow` so it does not compete with production.

## Non-negotiables

1. **One origin** — All canonicals, sitemap locs, OG `url`, JSON-LD `url`/`@id`, and robots `Sitemap:` use `getSiteUrl()` → production `https://www.onetap-card.com`. Never hardcode `https://onetap-card.com`.
2. **Dynamic discovery** — `/sitemap.xml` from `src/app/sitemap.ts`; `/robots.txt` from `src/app/robots.ts`. Do **not** add stale `public/sitemap.xml` or `public/robots.txt`.
3. **Public pages are discoverable** — New indexable routes: `buildLocaleMetadata` (or blog equivalent), both locales, sitemap static entry (blog slugs via `getAllSlugs()`), JSON-LD that matches **visible** copy.
4. **App surfaces stay out** — Dashboard, billing, editor, login live on the app host. Do not add them to the marketing sitemap.
5. **GEO files stay truthful** — Primary landing add/remove must update `/llms.txt` in the same PR.
6. **Preview never competes** — Do not weaken preview `Disallow` / `noindex` to “test SEO on preview.”

## Schema map

| Surface | Schema |
|---|---|
| Locale chrome | `Organization` + `WebSite` |
| Home | `SoftwareApplication` |
| `/faq` only | `FAQPage` (do not duplicate on homepage FAQ section) |
| Blog posts | `BlogPosting` |
| Nested landings / blog | `BreadcrumbList` |

Helpers: `src/lib/seo/json-ld.ts` + `<JsonLd />`.

## AI crawl policy

Default is **allow** citation crawlers in `robots.ts`. Blocking GPTBot/Claude/Perplexity is an explicit legal/product decision — not a drive-by PR change.
